From 4559c68d6132541b436a6f9f60138adb64bb40a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jihad Hanna <jihadghanna@google.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:33:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Do not hold RenderFrame pointers across synchronous
 layout updates

Calls that force style and layout updates (such as
WebElement::BoundsInWidget() and
WebFrameWidget::CalculateSelectionBounds()) can synchronously trigger
fallback content rendering on an embedding <object> element, which
detaches the child frame and destroys its content::RenderFrameImpl.

To prevent use-after-free of content::RenderFrame across layout updates:
- Compute BoundsInWidget() before resolving and null-checking the
  content::RenderFrame in WebFormControlElementToFormField(),
  FindFormForContentEditable(), PasswordAutofillAgent, and
  PasswordGenerationAgent.
- Change WebFormControlElementToFormField() to return
  std::optional<FormFieldData> and return std::nullopt when the frame is
  detached during layout.
- Update AutofillAgent::GetCaretBounds() to resolve
  unsafe_render_frame() after CalculateSelectionBounds().
- Do not cache unsafe_render_frame() across FormCache::UpdateFormCache()
  in AutofillAgent::ExtractFormsUnthrottled().

